// Per-process arenas (EmoOS T5.1): every spawned process allocates
// against its own arena — a 64 KiB carve from the root's heap at
// spawn — and a runaway child dies alone: its allocator reports and
// ends it, and the root continues. The lanes refuse on every hosted
// target's quota story (the interpreter has no arenas); this corpus
// runs on the freestanding image under QEMU alone.
//
//   emo build main.emo --target riscv64

// A runaway: a million boxes against a 64 KiB arena. The 2049th
// allocation finds the carve full; the allocator prints and ends this
// process, and the machine goes on without it.
def burn(n Int64) Void {
  var i = 0
  while i < n {
    var b = Box.new(i)
    i = i + 1
  }
}

println("spawned")
const kid = do burn(1000000)
// The send yields the root, so the child runs now: it burns its carve
// and dies inside it — the allocator's report (the one line the
// runtime prints, `heap gone in process 2`) lands before the root's
// next line. The message stays queued in a dead process's mailbox,
// and the root resumes.
kid <- 1
println("survived")
println(kid)
